  "task": {
    "objective": "Each grower earns fruit only from ripe own plots. They share three mobile pollinators, three circulating seeds and 22 initial water units, creating individual incentives to coordinate flowering and habitat care while competing for resources and six season harvest slots.",
    "natural_termination": "The sixth accepted harvest ends the season; cyclic transaction order allocates a final scarce harvest slot without exceeding six. The season can also end when no water remains in any storage and no ripe fruit remains. Otherwise time ends at 96 transitions.",
    "interaction": "Every flowering plot changes the shared pollinators destination set. A bee carries the last visited owner label; visiting a different owner flower raises its future fruit from one to three. Habitat water restores bee visit capacity and is shared across owners. Water draws, neighbor irrigation and physical seed gifts transfer actual scarce resources; there is no cooperation-label reward.",
    "observation_access": "The world is fully observable: all positions, owners, seed/water balances, growth clocks, pollination/fruit state, pollinator memory/targets, habitat reserves and tank balance are public native fields. Own role is an explicit one-hot. Every scene entity uses true public visibility; there is no private renderer-only plant or bee state."
  },
