  "action_resolution": "All thirteen intent actions are legal before joint termination; missing range, ownership, capacity or inventory prerequisites cause deterministic no-ops. Invalid indices map to 0; terminal calls allow only 0. Simultaneous movement blocks walls, input occupied cells and duplicate destinations; swaps are blocked. Resource transactions use cyclic grower priority starting at t mod 3, with nearest admissible target and lowest id ties. Only own plots can be planted, harvested or uprooted; anyone may water another plot or maintain habitat. Pollinators are processed in id order for finite habitat-water withdrawals. A tick completes its physics even when its sixth harvest has been accepted.",
  "rng_contract": "Reset is deterministic and does not consume its supplied key. Each live step draws phases=jax.random.randint(step_key,(3,),0,6,dtype=int32). Each phase breaks equal-distance flower ties by cyclic plot rank and chooses x-first versus y-first movement when both are possible. No other random source or stored key is used. Paired interventions require the same literal per-step keys so differences are not caused by reseeding.",
  "event_visibility_note": "All entities and event participants are public. Per-step planting, irrigation, visit, pollination, ripening and harvesting flags are distinct from persistent stages, fruit levels, soil water and pollination flags. Habitat maintenance events denote grower deposits; bee refill consumption is visible as actual reserve changes, not falsely labelled new maintenance.",
